currence (equivalently the continuant K_n(h,...,h)), not Morgan--Voyce. Morgan--Voyce B_n and b_n both satisfy the MINUS-sign three-term recurrence B_n = (x+2)B_{n-1} - B_{n-2}, i.e. B_n(x) = U_n(1 + x/2) — the very Chebyshev shape this block contrasts itself against. Computed b_3 = h^2+1, b_4 = h^3+2h, b_5 = h^4+3h^2+1, b_6 = h^5+4h^3+3h, b_7 = h^6+5h^4+6h^2+1, which are sympy's fibonacci(n, h) exactly. Likely origin of the slip: Morgan--Voyce evaluated at x=1 gives the odd-index Fibonacci NUMBERS, b_n(1)=F_{2n+1}. Proposed: name the family 'Fibonacci polynomials F_n(h)' or 'the continuant K_n(h,...,h)' throughout (this block, its proof, and rem:lepton-continuant-recurrence-novelty). (2) The stated contrast with Chebyshev is a change of variable, not a structural distinction: verified symbolically for n=1..7 that F_n(x) = (-i)^{n-1} U_{n-1}(i x / 2). The plus-sign family is Chebyshev U at imaginary argument. See the fail recorded on rem:lepton-continuant-recurrence-novelty, whose entire content is that contrast.","history":2},{"id":"trap-nonspeakable","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["ts"],"at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:l00","notes":"no trap of this class; full-context read","history":2},{"id":"trap-performed-warmth","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["ts"],"at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:l00","notes":"no trap of this class; full-context read","history":2},{"id":"trap-rhetorical-pivot","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["ts"],"at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:l00","notes":"no trap of this class; full-context read","history":2},{"id":"trap-superlative","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["ts"],"at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:l00","notes":"no trap of this class; full-context read","history":2},{"id":"trap-thesis-restatement","group":"trap","re